summary:
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: The board announced it has identified a preferred candidate for the superintendent
    position and unanimously voted to authorize the chair to enter into contract negotiations.
    A public announcement is pending the conclusion of these negotiations.
- topic: Board Member Recognition
  text: The board honored departing student representatives Alex Davidson and Angel
    Kabisa for their service, with members expressing gratitude for their valuable
    insights and contributions during a challenging period.
- topic: Student Recognition
  text: The board celebrated the South Portland High School Top Scholars for 2026.
    The ceremony featured students introducing their peers and sharing their academic
    achievements, extracurricular involvement, and future university and career plans.
- topic: Personnel
  text: As part of the consent agenda, the board approved the issuance of numerous
    secondary probationary and first continuing contracts for teachers and staff.
    The superintendent also announced several resignations, including the principal
    of Kaler Elementary School.
- topic: Elementary Reconfiguration & Kaler Closure
  text: An update was provided on the 23-member elementary reconfiguration steering
    committee, confirming its meetings are open to the public. Regarding the Kaler
    Elementary School closure, a parent survey was distributed to gather input on
    student placement priorities for the upcoming school year.
- topic: Financial Report
  text: The Finance Committee reported a lowered projected deficit range for the current
    fiscal year, aided by additional MaineCare revenue. The city council has approved
    up to $2 million in debt forgiveness for the district if needed.
- topic: Policy Updates
  text: 'The board conducted first readings for two policies: Policy BEDB concerning
    the meeting agenda, and a new Educational Equity Policy, which includes a detailed
    procedures component.'
- topic: Transportation Safety
  text: During public comment, parents and a transportation employee raised significant
    safety concerns about severe overcrowding on buses for athletic events and regular
    morning routes, with students reportedly sitting in aisles. The superintendent
    pledged to investigate the issue immediately.
